Licensing and attribution for the released data
===============================================

This file covers everything under data/ — the three benchmark tiers, the tier
databases, the benchmark slices and the cached geocoder predictions. The
software is under the MIT licence; see LICENSE.

The data has three distinct origins and they carry different terms.


1. OpenStreetMap-derived fields — ODbL 1.0
------------------------------------------

  © OpenStreetMap contributors
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

7,842 records in the gold and silver tiers were verified against
OpenStreetMap, drawn from 7,689 distinct OSM ways. For those records the
following fields, nested under `aux.existence` where `aux.existence.source`
is `"osd"`, are derived from OpenStreetMap and are made available under the
Open Database License 1.0:

  osm_id          the OSM way identifier, retained so provenance is explicit
  street_name     the street name as it appears in OpenStreetMap
  geometry        the way geometry, as WKT LINESTRING
  country, province, county, city, district, suburb, postal_code and the
                  other administrative fields of the same object

The ODbL text is at https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Street extraction follows the method published at https://openstreetdata.org

Any redistribution of these fields, or of a database derived from them, must
preserve this attribution and the ODbL terms.


2. OpenAddresses-derived fields — per-source terms
--------------------------------------------------

  https://openaddresses.io/

12,158 records were verified against OpenAddresses instead. For those, the
fields nested under `aux.existence` where `aux.existence.source` is `"oa"`
are derived from OpenAddresses. OpenAddresses aggregates government and other
open sources whose licences differ by source; each record retains its
`oa_source` field so the originating source can be identified, and its terms
consulted.


3. The address records themselves — Web Data Commons
-----------------------------------------------------

  http://webdatacommons.org/structureddata/

The 30,000 address records are extracted verbatim from the December 2024 Web
Data Commons corpus, which is itself derived from Common Crawl. They are
published here for research use, in the form in which they appeared on the
web.

Records were filtered by a language model for personally identifiable
information across all six address fields before release; the candidates that
filter rejected are not included in this distribution.


Status of the ODbL classification
---------------------------------

A request was sent to the OpenStreetMap Foundation Licensing Working Group on
20 August 2026 asking whether this arrangement — full attribution and an
explicit ODbL notice on the OSM-derived fields, with way identifiers retained
— is compliant as described. No response has been received at the time of
writing. This file states the plan that was put to them; it will be updated if
their answer calls for a change.
